---
import EditorialFrame from '../../components/EditorialFrame.astro';
import { services, fmtDate } from '../../lib/data.js';
import { newestDate } from '../../lib/editorial.js';

const service = services.NZ.get('fee-paying-student-visa');
const p50 = service.percent50;
const p80 = service.percent80;
const pathway = services.NZ.get('pathway-student-visa');
const reviewedStudentVisas = [service, pathway];
const officialVisa = 'https://www.immigration.govt.nz/visas/fee-paying-student-visa/';
const officialPathwayVisa = 'https://www.immigration.govt.nz/visas/pathway-student-visa/';
---
<EditorialFrame
  sectionName="Guides"
  sectionPath="/guides/"
  slug="new-zealand-student-visa-processing-time"
  title="New Zealand Student Visa Processing Times: Current INZ Data"
  description="Compare current INZ processing times for Fee Paying and Pathway Student Visas, including 50% and 80% working-day figures and source-backed history."
  h1="New Zealand student visa processing times"
  lede={`Immigration New Zealand currently reports separate processing-time distributions for Fee Paying and Pathway Student Visas. Both reviewed routes currently show 50% within ${p50.value_raw} and 80% within ${p80.value_raw}, but GovWait keeps their histories separate because they are different visa categories.`}
  modified={newestDate('2026-10-02', service.latestEffective, pathway.latestEffective)}
  checked={newestDate(service.latestEffective, pathway.latestEffective)}
  about={['New Zealand student visa', 'Fee Paying Student Visa', 'Pathway Student Visa', 'INZ processing times']}
  citations={[officialVisa, officialPathwayVisa, p80.source_url, pathway.percent80.source_url]}
  adPrefix="guide-nz-student"
>
  <div class="stats"><div><div class="n">{reviewedStudentVisas.length}</div><div class="l">reviewed student routes</div></div><div><div class="n">{p50.value_raw}</div><div class="l">current 50% point for both</div></div><div><div class="n">{p80.value_raw}</div><div class="l">current 80% point for both</div></div></div>

  <h2>Current reviewed student-visa comparison</h2>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Visa</th><th>50% processed</th><th>80% processed</th></tr></thead><tbody>{reviewedStudentVisas.map(item => (<tr><td><a href={`/new-zealand/${item.slug}/`}>{item.name}</a></td><td>{item.percent50.value_raw}</td><td>{item.percent80.value_raw}</td></tr>))}</tbody></table></div>
  <p>The matching values are a current coincidence, not permission to merge the routes. Each official visa has its own eligibility rules and keeps its own append-only GovWait history.</p>

  <h2>Why the 80% figure is important for study planning</h2>
  <p>The 50% point describes the middle of the represented applications; it does not describe the slower half. The 80% point reaches farther into that distribution, while still leaving one in five represented applications beyond it. A student planning around only the first number discards that uncertainty.</p>

  <h2>Working days are not calendar days</h2>
  <p>INZ excludes Saturdays, Sundays and New Zealand public holidays from its working-day measure. GovWait preserves the published working-day counts rather than converting them to a calendar date that could be wrong for the submission date and holiday period.</p>

  <h2>Keep three planning periods separate</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Before application:</strong> admission, tuition or funding evidence, supporting documents and any other official prerequisites take their own time.</li>
    <li><strong>Visa processing:</strong> the current INZ distribution is {p50.value_raw} at 50% and {p80.value_raw} at 80%.</li>
    <li><strong>After decision:</strong> travel, accommodation, course-start and other arrangements remain separate.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>The official visa page—not this guide—defines the current eligibility and document requirements.</p>

  <h2>What can extend an application</h2>
  <p>INZ explains that incomplete or complex applications, requests for information, verification and demand can increase the wait. A complete file may sit closer to the average, but the published figures do not guarantee that result.</p>
  <div class="callout warn"><strong>Course dates and visa dates are not interchangeable.</strong> Use the school’s instructions and INZ’s official guidance, and avoid treating the 50% point as a safe latest-submission date.</div>

  <h2>History and wider comparison</h2>
  <p>The <a href="/new-zealand/fee-paying-student-visa/">Fee Paying Student Visa page</a> and <a href="/new-zealand/pathway-student-visa/">Pathway Student Visa page</a> keep their 50% and 80% values as separate append-only series. The <a href="/reports/new-zealand-visa-processing-time-changes/">New Zealand report</a> compares their gap with other reviewed visas and will identify later verified changes.</p>

  <h2>Common questions</h2>
  <h3>Can {p50.value_raw} be converted to an exact decision date?</h3><p>No. It is a distribution point in working days and half of represented applications took longer.</p>
  <h3>Does the 80% figure cover every application?</h3><p>No. By definition, the remaining 20% are outside that completion point.</p>
  <div class="prov">Official sources: <a href={officialVisa} rel="noopener">Fee Paying Student Visa</a>, <a href={officialPathwayVisa} rel="noopener">Pathway Student Visa</a> and the <a href={p80.source_url} rel="noopener">INZ processing-time tool</a> · values first observed {fmtDate(newestDate(service.latestEffective, pathway.latestEffective))}.</div>
</EditorialFrame>
